  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C8 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">When words are not reaching your child in the middle of a meltdown, the body can offer another route to calm.<br><br>Slow, firm input, a snug hug, a weighted blanket, a steady squeeze on the shoulders, helps engage the calming branch of the nervous system, the one that brings a revved-up body back down out of high alert. It works below language, through the body directly, which is exactly why it can land when talking is bouncing right off.<br><br>So when your child is too flooded for words, connecting through the body first is not giving up on communication. It is using a different, often faster, door to calm. Offer it, watch what your child actually welcomes, and let their body lead. The body has its own route to calm.</div>
